OL,3,ATiny image sparks big backlash in Nikon
OL,4,Aphoto contest
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe winning entry of a prestigious
OL,7,Fscientific photography competition is
OL,8,Fbeing re-evaluated following criticism
OL,9,Ffrom other scientists that it was made
OL,10,Fwith AI.
OL,12,FNikon's annual Small World In Motion
OL,13,Fcontest accepts photos and video taken
OL,14,Fusing powerful microscopes, and has run
OL,15,Fannually for the last 15 years.
OL,17,FThe winner was a short video submitted
OL,18,Fby Dr Ning Xu, a researcher at Tsinghua
OL,19,FUniversity in China, which claims to be
OL,20,Ffootage of tiny, hair-like structures
OL,21,Fcalled cilia moving inside the airways
OL,22,Fof a child with a rare disease.
OL,23,APub: 30-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/18
